{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793351192,"nonce":"gcuopEl6iflJ11qZQeT04g4cwtg=","title":"Complete Ashui Tw utility classes and style helpers","message":"Add context-aware Rayzor LSP completion for Ashui's Tailwind-style utilities in HXX class literals and calls to ashui.style.Tw.tw, including an imported tw helper. Also preserve ordinary public Tw member/signature/documentation completion and respect @:noCompletion for internal helpers. Resolve helper identity through imports and types rather than matching an arbitrary function named tw.\n\nAshui's haxe/ashui/style/Tw.hx generates utilities from theme token enums and combines them with layout/CSS keywords, supported state variants, color opacity suffixes and a limited arbitrary-value grammar. The compiler's accepted vocabulary should supply completion metadata. Do not ship an unrelated Tailwind catalog or copy Tw's private Expr-producing vocabulary into Rayzor.\n\nExpected behavior:\n- Complete the current whitespace-delimited class token inside class=\"...\" and Tw.tw(\"...\") / tw(\"...\") without replacing neighboring classes, quotes or Haxe expressions. Support an unfinished token or string.\n- Offer the token-derived spacing, color, typography, radius, shadow and motion utilities and the other keyword families actually supported by Tw, with concise property/value documentation where available.\n- Complete valid variants such as hover:, focus-visible:, dark:, group-* and peer-* using Tw's own restrictions. Tw currently accepts one variant per class; completion must not invent unsupported stacked variants.\n- Handle supported color opacity suffixes and snippet forms for the permitted [clip-path:...] and [glass-*:...] values. Do not suggest arbitrary Tailwind forms that Ashui rejects.\n- Distinguish HXX class contexts, where authored CSS classes can coexist, from the tw style helper's accepted utility vocabulary. Leave unrelated strings alone.\n- Use cached, library-owned plain completion descriptors shared with HXX completion. Keep queries available before full indexing; avoid executing style generation or building UI nodes during completion. Invalidate on token/library/project-define changes.\n\nVerification: completion and edit ranges for multiple tokens, incomplete strings, prefixes/variants, theme-derived utilities, qualified/imported helper calls, hidden internal members and unrelated strings; cold/warm BLADE parity; an Ashui-side consistency check that offered utilities/variants agree with Tw's actual parser. This is tracked work, not an implementation in this change.\n\nOwnership: Rayzor provides string/context completion and protocol handling; Ashui exposes its vocabulary, token documentation and supported grammar through the shared metadata interface. Implement alongside the HXX tag/prop completion task.","files":null}]}